But wait, we need to be careful. The check reads until null. If buf[0] = 0, check passes. Then the rest of buf (bytes 1 to 0x77) and the return address area can be arbitrary.

Actually, let me reconsider the whole thing. The simplest exploit: just put a null byte at the start, then pad to 0x78, then ROP chain to call system("/bin/sh") or similar.

